002518                    ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
002519                    ; Building the map
002520                    ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
002521                    
002522                    ; SDB_MAP_BUILD
002523                    ; Walks the FAT cluster chain of an open file once and stores the result as
002524                    ; an extent table, so that SDB_LBA can map blocks to LBAs afterwards. Costs
002525                    ; one SD card block read per 128 clusters of the file.
002526                    ;
002527                    ; Reads FAT sectors directly and therefore destroys the FAT32 library's
002528                    ; sector buffer, so it guards and restores it (see THE TWO RULES above). It
002529                    ; never modifies the file handle: the file position is the same afterwards.
002530                    ;
002531                    ; Input: R8: file handle (FDH)
002532                    ; R9: pointer to the block map to be filled
002533                    ; Output: none. The map is left invalid (extent count = 0, reason in
002534                    ; SDB_M_BAIL) when the file cannot be described, which makes all
002535                    ; callers fall back silently.
002536  8688  FF90  005E  SDB_MAP_BUILD               ASUB enter, 1
002537                    
002538  868A  0800                                    MOVE R8, R0                      ; R0: FDH
002539  868B  0904                                    MOVE R9, R1                      ; R1: map
002540                    
002541  868C  0F85  0000                              MOVE 0, @R1                      ; invalid until proven good
002542  868E  0108                                    MOVE R1, R2
002543  868F  1F88  0004                              ADD SDB_M_BAIL, R2
